# Prefer MCP corpora over guessing

When answering questions about Paragon Cursor guides, Technical Architecture docs, or Abbey View wiki content, use the Paragon Knowledge MCP tools before inventing facts.

## Required behavior

1. Inventory with `list_corpora` when unsure what is loaded.
2. Search with `search_docs`; fetch with `get_doc` / `get_doc_metadata` using corpus paths (`user-guide/...`, `tech-arch/...`, `abbey-view/...`).
3. Cite the corpus path you used. If search returns an unavailable-title notice, report that honestly; do not fabricate a body.
4. Diagram labels may only appear under `## Extracted diagram text` (OCR). Treat OCR accuracy as variable. When a tool result includes `diagramOcr` / `unreadDiagrams`, tell the user that referenced diagrams could not be read and answers based only on prose may be incomplete.
5. Do not claim content exists in a corpus that is not loaded or configured.

## Out of scope

- General programming help unrelated to these corpora.
- Editing live SharePoint or wiki binaries; convert to Markdown first via approved ParaDOCS / convert tooling.
